  ITEM black "The component of the story that tells *where* the story happens is called the *Place.* This can be real or imaginary."
  ITEM black "The component of the story that tells *when* the story happens is called the *Time.* This can be general – in the past, present or future – or it can be specific – 74 Queen Street, Auckland on the evening of December 24th."
  ITEM black "The setting of a story influences the characters and plot of a story. For example, a story that takes place in the futuristic city of Agen will be very different from a story that takes place in a Māori pā in 1810."
