  OUT <div class="row carousel"> <div class="col-md-12 col-12 viewer"> <div class="item"> <div class="videoSection ratio ratio-16x9"> <iframe src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/1T6PmQQlKss" loading="lazy" title="YouTube video player" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe> </div> </div> <div class="item"> <h4>Revising Your Story</h4> <div class="carousel-caption"> <p>Revising is making changes to your story to improve it.</p> <p>It could involve:</p> <ul> <li>adding information or details to your story</li> <li>changing parts of your story to make them more interesting and descriptive</li> <li>removing words or details that don’t make sense or are unnecessary.</li> </ul> <p>The first step is to reread your story, one part at a time. As you do this, try to think about it from a reader’s perspective.</p> <p>Ask yourself:</p> <ul> <li>Does each sentence and part make sense?</li> <li>Is it interesting?</li> <li>Can I add more detail to make it better?</li> <li>Are there words I can swap out for more precise, descriptive words?</li> <li>Are there places where I need to apply my <i>Show, Don’t Tell</i> skills?</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div> </div>
